# Publish to the public registry regardless of any user- or machine-level
# override. A corporate mirror in ~/.npmrc is a normal thing to have, and
# without this an `npm publish` here would push Felix at an internal feed --
# or fail against one, which is how we found out.
#
# The publish script passes --registry as well. That flag is what actually
# holds, because npm reads the .npmrc of the directory it runs in and each
# platform package is its own directory.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
